  "scope": "The terrain JSON v4 writer sizes and fills one output allocation. Its independent ordinary request observation matches that allocation and a 64-byte numeric formatting buffer is on the stack. Empty, sparse and dense files match the v4 byte reference, including full-width IDs, packed fluid, signed coordinates and floating-point terrain weather. The single allocation refusal retires all backing and the retry emits the same bytes. Flat confirms physical async write and synchronous reload of 4096 voxels.",
